  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Allowed region C(σ)Matching colors = matching inputs"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "point-condition",
   "text": "x has support {a,b,c}. Its image is outside C({a,b,c})."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Select a face, then drag x. The condition must hold for every face and every point."
  },
  {
   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Why? / The definition"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "A carrier assigns regions, not individual output points. For each nonempty face σ, C(σ) is a subspace of Y. Smaller faces must receive smaller allowed regions: τ ⊆ σ ⇒ C(τ) ⊆ C(σ)."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "A continuous map f: |Δ| → Y is carried when f(⟨σ⟩) ⊆ C(σ) for every nonempty face σ. Neither the carrier regions nor the images have to equal Y."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "case-explanation",
   "text": "The map is the ordinary affine map plus a vertical bump 1.05·27λₐλᵦλ𝚌. That bump vanishes on the entire boundary, but pushes the barycenter above the allowed triangle. All outputs remain in Y. The full two-dimensional face must be checked too."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Source: Björner, Nerves, fibers and homotopy groups, p. 89 (Carrier Lemma)."
  },
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Source: Björner, Nerves, fibers and homotopy groups, p. 89 (Carrier Lemma)."
  }
